      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A report is only as good as your notes. Vague words, missing photos and actions with no owner are the usual faults. They all come from writing it up from memory at the van.</p><p>This guide shows how to write a site inspection report that holds up. It covers what to include, where reports go wrong, and what clear notes look like.</p><p>Quickler writes the report from the voice notes and photos you send as you walk, so it is ready when you leave site. Graeme Clark at Ethos Safety went from 1 to 2 hours of write-up to 14 minutes on average. If you are an H&amp;S consultant, see <a href=\"/pages/health-and-safety-consultants.html\">how to spend less time writing health and safety reports</a>.</p>"
    },
